{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1137445-help-statting-out-my-big-bads","id":1137445,"title":"Help statting out my Big Bads?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-09-04T14:20:34-07:00","id":1137445,"title":"Help statting out my Big Bads?","content":"I need some help statting up the Big Bads for my M20 game. They're Demon-Gods Who have been stuck in a power draining otherworld for thousands of years, thus rendering them killable. There are seven of them based on my version of the Elements( the standard 4 plus spirit, time and space). I'm not even sure at the moment if they are physical or possessing entities. They need to be powerful enough to give my players a run for their money without being unbeatable. My players are very creative and all at Arete 4, and there are 4 of them. Please help!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10179-shadryx","name":"shadryx","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-04T14:25:06-07:00","id":1137449,"title":"","content":"They're also connected to the 7 deadly sins.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10179-shadryx","name":"shadryx","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-04T14:49:37-07:00","id":1137458,"title":"","content":"Can you provide more information about these Demon-Gods?<br /> Like for example their names, and to which of the elements, and to which of the seven sins, each one is is connected.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 09-04-2017, 05:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-04T17:50:20-07:00","id":1137524,"title":"","content":"fire/wrath, air/envy, water/lust, earth/sloth, spirit/pride, time/greed, and space/gluttony. They've been locked away for so long even they don't remember their original names. They escaped their prison about thirteen years ago and now have some Nephandi cultists they are using as disposable minions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10179-shadryx","name":"shadryx","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-06T06:53:15-07:00","id":1138009,"title":"","content":"It's kind of easy with the classical elements. Earth/Sloth would be a strong tanky type, the one who charges in head first and uses some kind of grab attack but is really really slow, so the players have some time to react. Water uses mind control or minions to fight for her. She could have some buffs to those under her sway (ignore health penalties or something along the way). Air/Envy is really fast and attacks multiple times per turn, but has difficultys focusing on one target, nerfing her down a bit. And Fire would be a powerfull but not as durable fighter, dealing aggravated damage.<br /> <br /> It's difficult to really balance these antagonists, as long as we don't know if they are always alone or fighting together.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13221,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13221-thevarulfen","user":"TheVarulfen","date":". 09-06-2017, 09:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13221-thevarulfen","name":"TheVarulfen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-06T07:03:05-07:00","id":1138010,"title":"","content":"Spirit/Pride: Enhances a possessed body. Give him some Fomor powers, but make them less disfiguring and more like a real enhancement.<br /> <br /> Time/Greed: Maybe have him deal some damage to a random character on the end of each turn. Make it a dice throw and on a botch, he's hitting himself. It's some time magic that summons up future damage the character may take at any time. (And maybe write down who was hit, so he may negate that damage later on. He already suffered it by then.<br /> <br /> Space/Gluttony: Some Fullmetal Alchemist vibes here (also with Sloth). Maybe this one's less about a direct fight and more like a &quot;Find his heart in his inner dimension.&quot;-Quest. Let the characters confront him. They get eaten by his deus ex machina powers and now they have to find a way out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13221-thevarulfen","name":"TheVarulfen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-06T11:50:50-07:00","id":1138061,"title":"","content":"I really like these Ideas, Varulfen, I think I'll run with it!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10179-shadryx","name":"shadryx","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-06T11:53:40-07:00","id":1138062,"title":"","content":"They have nothing to do with each other. They've been imprisoned together for so long they can't stand the sight of each other. They do use Nephandi cultists as cannon fodder, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10179-shadryx","name":"shadryx","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-06T11:55:16-07:00","id":1138063,"title":"","content":"I think I'll have them possess bodies and warp them to fit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10179-shadryx","name":"shadryx","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}